 "caption": {
  "instagram": "How to stay consistent with a workout plan: plan for your real week, not a perfect one.\n\nWhy we stop doing things we know are good for us, reason #18: the perfect week. We plan seven runs, real life gives us four, and four out of seven reads as a fail. A few weeks of \"failing\" and we quit, even though four runs a week is good.\n\nThe fix:\n- Count what you actually did in the last two weeks\n- That number is your plan\n- Hit it two weeks in a row? Add one\n\nSame four runs, now a hundred percent, and that's a week you want to repeat.\n\nHow many days did you really manage last week? Tell me below.\n\nDmyor: archive your dream today, break it into steps you can actually do. Link in bio.",
